@group
    @title=TREECLASSMATCH template
    @brief=The section describes the template that compares two classes set in different docgen models
    @ingroup=templates
    @key=treeclassmatch

    The template is useful when the documentation is created using [link=cs2dsTemplate]C# to docgen[/link]
    or [link=doxigen2dsTemplate]Doxygen to docgen[/link] to create the documentation skeleton which then
    was modified by the documentation writer. When code changes the task to find which classes and methods
    are added or removed or which signatures are changed may become challenging. This template allows to compare
    the documentation source and auto-generated tree in order to find these situations.

    Please not that this assembly does NOT use [link=modelXML]DocGen XML document[/link]
    as a source. It opens and processes the document specified
    in the template parameters. However, because it is still required to have
    any DocGen XML document, you have to create a source file with an
    empty index group, e.g. and specify it as a source for your
    [link=docProjectFile]docgen project[/link].

    To provide initial data for the template you should parse two sets of docgen source files and
    save them using [clink=nullTemplate]nullTemplate[/clink] as XML files. You will need two
    separate docgen projects to do that.

    @example
        @show=always
        @gray=yes
    !@group
    !    @title=Index
    !    @brief=
    !    @key=main
    !    @ingroup=
    !@end
    @end

    The template is located at
    `%docgen%/template/treeclassmatch/main.xsl`

    ```xml
    <dg:output template="%docgen%/template/treeclassmatch/main.xsl" file="comparison.xml" encoding="utf-8">
    ```

    The template has following parameters:

    @table
        @width=100%
        @row
            @header=yes
            @col
                @width=30%
                Parameter
            @end
            @col
                Description
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `model1`
            @end
            @col
                The first XML model to compare
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `model2`
            @end
            @col
                The second XML model to compare
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `member-find-mode`
            @end
            @col
                `name` or `key`.

                The flag defines the method how the template finds the methods by the name or by the key.

                If the documentation is build using newer templates (post 1.10 for C# and post 1.17 for C++ and Java)
                the key for the member is build from the member signature and it is suggested to use the `key` option.

                Earlier documentation may have key which does not depend on the member signature so `name` option
                would be more efficient.
            @end
        @end
        @row
            @col
                `compare-parameters`
            @end
            @col
                `yes` or `no`.

                If methods are found using `key`, the key itself already reflects the whole signature, so you don't have
                to compare parameters separately. However, if the methods are found using `name` you may
                want to use this option to detect the situation when the parameter set is changed.
            @end
        @end
    @end

    The template is introduced in docgen 0.1.17.
@end
